\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The simplest Ginsparg–Wilson operators}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{For #{D=0}, the quadratic relation holds and the
[modified grading](fdip-0148) equals #{\Gamma}. For
#{D=a^{-1}(\bbI-\Gamma)}, the positive grading space is the
kernel and the negative space has eigenvalue #{2a^{-1}}.
The operator is self-adjoint and commutes with #{\Gamma}.
On the negative space both sides of the relation are
#{-4a^{-1}\bbI}, and both vanish on the positive space.
Here #{\Gamma'=\bbI}. Taking #{K=-\Gamma} gives
#{\Gamma K=-\bbI} and #{\Gamma_K=-\bbI}, so the overlap formula
also gives this #{D}.}
